{
  "comment": [
    "What Flyway reaches by name at run time when StreamRune initializes the schema",
    "(streamrune.event-store.schema.auto-initialize). A Quarkus native build registers no",
    "ServiceLoader provider on its own and does not apply the GraalVM reachability-metadata",
    "repository, so the integration lists it. FlywayNativeImageMetadataTest checks every entry",
    "against the Flyway on the class path.",
    "resources: Flyway finds its plugins, the PostgreSQL database type among them, with",
    "ServiceLoader.load(Plugin.class), which reads the provider names from this file.",
    "reflection, a type with <init>: a plugin that file names; ServiceLoader instantiates each",
    "through its no-argument constructor and fails the whole lookup when one cannot be loaded.",
    "reflection, a type with allDeclaredFields: a configuration extension Flyway copies with",
    "getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance() and a field-by-field copy (MergeUtils.copyModel).",
    "reflection, Slf4jLogCreator: StreamRune tells Flyway to log through SLF4J, and Flyway",
    "instantiates the log creator from its class name."
  ],
